cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SAICA-Bench, its results or the SAICA-KG data, please cite it as below, with the results version."
title: SAICA-Bench
abstract: >-
  SAICA-Bench measures whether supervision tools and language models catch
  typical failures in the output of AI coding agents (fabrication, test
  manipulation, security vulnerabilities, logic errors, incomplete execution,
  scope creep, obsolescence, supply-chain attacks, dependency blindness).
  Every reviewer sees the same labelled samples and is scored J = TPR - FPR
  within one failure mode, with a 95% interval and the cost per 1,000
  reviews. Results are grouped by how the samples were made: real agent
  output, model-written code, and failures planted on purpose. Models asked
  directly are told which failure to look for, so their scores are
  mode-primed estimates. The repository also holds SAICA-KG, the catalog of
  failure modes, supervision tools, papers, incidents and external
  taxonomies behind the benchmark. Code: Apache-2.0; annotations and
  results: CC-BY-4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
authors:
